# Input
```cjs
new Promise(async function foo(resolve, reject) {})
```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.jsonc:1:13 lint/suspicious/noAsyncPromiseExecutor ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × Promise executor functions should not be `async`.
  
  > 1 │ new Promise(async function foo(resolve, reject) {})
      │             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  
  i If an async executor throws or awaits a rejected promise, the error is not caught by the Promise constructor. The promise can stay pending forever.
  
  i Remove the async keyword and call resolve or reject instead. If you need await, run it outside the Promise constructor.
  

```

